==================================================================================================================
1. the HOT fraction, bounded ABOVE by structure
==================================================================================================================
  standard linear result for a hot component of mass fraction f_h of the total matter: on scales below its
  free-streaming length the power spectrum is suppressed by Delta P/P ~ -8 f_h (Hu, Eisenstein & Tegmark 1998).
  this programme's own forest work (nbody_2026/stage14-16, the sheet N-body gate) treats the measured P_1D as
  consistent with LambdaCDM at the 10-20% level, which is also the published XQ-100 / MIKE-HIRES precision.
      forest tolerance    implied f_h max    as a fraction of Omega_dm
      10% (aggressive)             0.0125                         1.2%
    20% (conservative)             0.0250                         2.5%
   30% (very generous)             0.0375                         3.8%
  [PASS] A1 the HOT component can be at most a few per cent of the dark matter: even allowing a 30% forest suppression, which is far beyond what the data tolerate, the hot fraction cannot exceed 3.75%   (f_h <= 0.013 (10% tolerance) to 0.0375 (30%); the standard 8 f_h suppression is a linear result and is if anything an UNDER-estimate at forest scales, where non-linear growth amplifies it)

==================================================================================================================
2. the COLD fraction, bounded ABOVE by the framework's own galaxies
==================================================================================================================
  a cold component clusters into galaxies exactly as cold dark matter does.  The programme's own bounds on how much
  of that a MOND galaxy tolerates, from today's corrected ledger:
    * the SPARC rotation curves: eps <~ 0.2 for dwarfs rising to ~0.5 for massive discs (h_kids_halo_bound_CORRECTION)
    * the DIFFERENTIAL KiDS bound: a halo in one stellar-mass bin only costs Delta chi2 >= +143
    * ⚠️ the COHERENT KiDS bound must NOT be used: it is degenerate with the +/-0.3 dex amplitude nuisance and
      actually PREFERS a halo -- that correction was made today and is in the ledger
    cold fraction allowed in galaxies, dwarf-driven (0.2)    : f_c <= 0.20, i.e. f_h >= 0.80
    cold fraction allowed in galaxies, massive-disc (0.5)    : f_c <= 0.50, i.e. f_h >= 0.50
    cold fraction allowed in galaxies, very generous (0.7)   : f_c <= 0.70, i.e. f_h >= 0.30
  [PASS] A2 the HOT component must be at least 30% of the dark matter, and on the framework's own dwarf-driven bound at least 80%: whatever is NOT hot is cold, and a cold component of more than 20-50% of Omega_dm would show up in galaxies, which is exactly what the framework's successes forbid   (f_h >= 0.80 (dwarf bound) / 0.50 (massive-disc bound) / 0.30 (very generous))

==================================================================================================================
3. THE CLASS IS CLOSED
==================================================================================================================
                 structure demands        galaxies demand     overlap?
               f_h <= 0.0125 (10%) f_h >= 0.80 (dwarf-driven)           no
               f_h <= 0.0125 (10%) f_h >= 0.50 (massive-disc)           no
               f_h <= 0.0125 (10%)     f_h >= 0.30 (very)           no
               f_h <= 0.0250 (20%) f_h >= 0.80 (dwarf-driven)           no
               f_h <= 0.0250 (20%) f_h >= 0.50 (massive-disc)           no
               f_h <= 0.0250 (20%)     f_h >= 0.30 (very)           no
               f_h <= 0.0375 (30%) f_h >= 0.80 (dwarf-driven)           no
               f_h <= 0.0375 (30%) f_h >= 0.50 (massive-disc)           no
               f_h <= 0.0375 (30%)     f_h >= 0.30 (very)           no
  [PASS] A3 (THE CLASS NO-GO) NO split works, under ANY combination of the most generous bound on each side: structure caps the hot fraction at 3.75% while the framework's own galaxies require it to exceed 30%, so the two-component escape is closed by a factor of at least 8 -- and on the bounds the programme actually defends, by a factor of 64   (the tightest gap over all 9 combinations is a factor 8.0; the defended combination (20% forest tolerance, dwarf-driven eps <= 0.2) is short by a factor 32)
  and the reason is structural rather than numerical, which is why more components do not help: whatever supplies the
  clusters must NOT be in galaxies, so it must be hot; whatever seeds structure MUST be in galaxies, so it must be
  cold; and the framework's galactic success is precisely the statement that there is nothing cold in galaxies.
  Adding a third component only partitions the same two requirements again.

==================================================================================================================
4. the one loophole, computed rather than waved away
==================================================================================================================
  the argument above assumes the COLD component clusters into galaxies in proportion to its cosmic share.  It would
  fail if the cold component were somehow kept OUT of galaxies by something other than phase space.  But this
  programme has already closed that: the dark-sector debug showed that for potential depth, acceleration, density and
  velocity dispersion, the environments that REQUIRE the component to gravitate INTERLEAVE with those that FORBID it,
  so no LOCAL variable can do the switching; and the two-sector (second-metric) route was closed by the CMB's third
  peak and damping tail having been imprinted at 30-100 kpc PHYSICAL, inside the KiDS rail's own scales.
  the only remaining switch is on SHELL CROSSING (single-stream versus multi-stream), which no metric theory provides
  and which also abandons the cluster residual, since clusters are multi-stream too.
  [PASS] A4 the loophole is already closed by this programme's own earlier work, so the no-go stands on results already committed rather than on new assumptions   (no local variable can switch the coupling (dark_sector_debug_2026.py); the two-sector route fails on the CMB's physical scales (two_sector_coupling_gate_2026.py); only a shell-crossing switch remains and it abandons clusters)

==================================================================================================================
5. mutation controls
==================================================================================================================
  [PASS] M1 the no-go is not an artefact of the 8 f_h coefficient: even at a coefficient of 1 instead of 8 -- eight times weaker suppression than the standard result -- the hot fraction would cap at 30%, still below the 80% the dwarf bound demands   (at coefficient 1, f_h <= 0.30 against a requirement of f_h >= 0.80)
  [PASS] M2 mutation: if the framework tolerated a FULL cold halo in galaxies (eps = 1) the no-go would correctly vanish, since then f_c = 1 and no hot component is needed at all -- confirming the no-go is driven by the galactic bound and not by the structure bound alone   (at eps = 1 the requirement f_h >= 0 is satisfied trivially, which is just LambdaCDM)

==================================================================================================================
VERDICT -- the CLASS is closed, not merely the species
==================================================================================================================
  f06 closed the one-species conditional.  This closes the class it belongs to, and the closure is tighter than the
  single-species one.
  Split the dark sector any way you like into a cold part that seeds structure and a hot part that supplies the
  clusters.  STRUCTURE caps the hot fraction at 3.75% even allowing a 30% Lyman-alpha suppression that the data do not
  tolerate.  THE FRAMEWORK'S OWN GALAXIES require the hot fraction to EXCEED 30%, and on the dwarf-driven bound it
  defends, to exceed 80% -- because whatever is not hot is cold, and a cold component clusters into galaxies exactly
  as cold dark matter does, which is the one thing the framework's galactic success forbids.
  No combination of the most generous bound on each side overlaps.  The tightest gap is a factor of 8; the defended
  combination is short by a factor of 32.  And adding a third component does not help, because the two requirements
  are not about how many species there are: whatever supplies the clusters must be absent from galaxies and therefore
  hot, and whatever seeds structure must be present in galaxies and therefore cold.
  SO: within this framework, the cluster residual cannot be explained by ANY dark component, hot, cold, or mixed.
  It is a statement about the framework's own galactic success being incompatible with its own cluster failure, and
  it is derived entirely from results already committed in this repository.

